{
 "content": [
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "De Morgan's Laws are a pair of very helpful formulas to convert from an expression of the probability of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": "and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": "of events into the probability of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": "or",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " of events (and vice versa). ",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "If, for example, you need the probability of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": "or ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": "and you know the events are independent (which makes the probability of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": "and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": "easy), you can use De Morgan's Law for or to first convert the ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": "or",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " expression into an ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "bold"
      }
     ],
     "text": "and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": "expression. ",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "de-morgans-law-for-or",
    "level": "3",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "De Morgan's Law for or",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "bold"
        },
        {
         "type": "italic"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Definition",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ": De Morgan's Law for ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "bold"
        },
        {
         "type": "italic"
        }
       ],
       "text": "or",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\P&(E_1 \\or E_2 \\or \\cdots E_n)\\\\\n&= 1 - \\P\\Big((E_1 \\or E_2 \\or \\cdots E_n)^C\\Big) \\\\\n&= 1 -\\P(E_1^C \\and E_2^C \\and \\cdots E_n^C)\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "One way to gain intuition is pictorially. Consider the events ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "F"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " depicted bellow. The area in white can either be expressed as ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\P(E \\or F)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " or as ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "1 - \\P(E^C \\and F^C)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "align": "center",
    "id": "b458b867-0e7e-42a7-863a-92bc3605e9d3",
    "naturalHeight": "664",
    "naturalWidth": "889",
    "src": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/probabilityforcs.firebasestorage.app/o/uploads%2Fimages%2Fb458b867-0e7e-42a7-863a-92bc3605e9d3?alt=media&token=7edc5c5a-079c-4f4f-9d1a-9a7e5546e6e9",
    "widthPct": "50"
   },
   "type": "kindImage"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "de-morgans-law-for-and",
    "level": "3",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "De Morgan's Law for and",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "bold"
        },
        {
         "type": "italic"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Definition",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ": De Morgan's Law for ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "bold"
        },
        {
         "type": "italic"
        }
       ],
       "text": "and",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\P&(E_1 \\and E_2 \\and \\cdots E_n)\\\\\n&= 1 - \\P\\Big((E_1 \\and E_2 \\and \\cdots E_n)^C\\Big) \\\\\n&= 1 -\\P(E_1^C \\or E_2^C \\or \\cdots E_n^C)\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Again, we can gain intuition from a picture of arbitrary events ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "E"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "F"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ". The area in white can be written as ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\P(E \\and F)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " or as ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "1 - \\p(E^C \\or F^C)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
